{{!-- EXPEDITIONS — a trip prepped before the night it is run: the regional map, the sites along
      the way, the monsters on the road, the page to read aloud when they arrive. Book I p.340
      ("What to prep", quoted in full on the walkthrough's opening step) is a list of DOCUMENTS to
      have ready, and this is where they are kept.

      THE SAME SHAPE AS THE ENCOUNTERS TAB, which is where the reasoning lives
      (gm-toolkit-tab-encounters.hbs): two lists out of one array split in JS off each card's
      `used` flag, never off the DOM; writes that do not go through the form, so no field carries
      a `name`; and one pencil beside the bar's New button guarding exactly the two delete buttons.

      WHAT IT IS NOT is the walkthrough's log. The "Run an Expedition" window keeps its own record
      of what happened on each trip — the route, the requirements they were told, what they
      carried — in a world setting, and Run on a card opens that window on this card's trip. Prep
      here; what was played is recorded there.

      THE SECOND OF THE PREP TAB'S THREE VIEWS (gm-toolkit-tab-prep.hbs), between Encounters and
      Sites, and a pane of that tab's own group (`data-group="prep"`) rather than the rail's.
      `tab expeditions` stays its class because `.tab.expeditions` is the scope of every listener
      and the drop zone gm-expeditions-tab.js binds — the thing that keeps a drop on an
      expedition card from being claimed by the Encounters engine, which prints the same class
      names one pane over.

      SITES ARE THEIR OWN VIEW NOW, the third segment of the switcher, having sat at the foot of
      this pane under a full card list. A site is what a trip is FOR, and that is exactly why it
      should not need a scroll past every trip to reach: the switcher puts the two one click
      apart, and the click is the same one a GM uses between any two kinds of prep.

      `data-tab="expeditions"` is also what earns the switcher segment its signpost glyph (the
      `.stonetop-gm-prep-view[data-tab]` rows in stonetop.css); the rail has no button by this
      name any more. --}}
<div class="tab expeditions steading-edit-section{{#if stonetop.prep.panes.expeditions.active}} active{{/if}}" data-group="prep" data-tab="expeditions"
     id="{{stonetop.prep.panes.expeditions.id}}" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="{{stonetop.prep.panes.expeditions.tabId}}">
	{{> "stonetop.steading-section-toggle" section="expeditions" editing=stonetop.edit.expeditions}}
	<section class="sheet-tab stonetop-gm-encounters{{#unless stonetop.edit.expeditions}} stonetop-gm-encounters--reading{{/unless}}">

		{{!-- THE PANE BAR, as on Encounters (gm-toolkit-tab-encounters.hbs): the lead, the "?"
		      that opens the full intro, and "New expedition" — moved into the empty state, and the bar drawn
		      `bare`, while the view has never held anything. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-pane-bar" kind="stonetop-gm-encounter"
		    lead=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.lead")
		    intro=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.intro")
		    pane=stonetop.prep.panes.expeditions
		    label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.add")
		    bare=(not (or stonetop.expeditions.active.length stonetop.expeditions.completed.length))}}

		{{!-- STRUGGLE AS ONE, called from here as well as from any character's Moves tab: it is the
		      move a journey reaches for most, and the GM is the one who calls it (Book I p.328). The
		      words come from module/struggle/struggle-view.js#struggleCallView, and change to "Open"
		      while one is under way, so a GM who closed its window can find it again. A player's roll
		      does not redraw this sheet, so the marked spans are rewritten in place as rolls land
		      (struggle-flow.js#refreshStruggleBars). --}}
		{{#if stonetop.struggle}}
		<div class="stonetop-gm-struggle-bar">
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-gm-struggle-call"><i class="fas fa-people-group" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span data-struggle-call-label>{{stonetop.struggle.label}}</span></button>
			<span class="stonetop-gm-struggle-hint" data-struggle-call-hint>{{stonetop.struggle.hint}}</span>
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{#if stonetop.expeditions.active.length}}
		<ul class="stonetop-gm-encounter-list">
			{{#each stonetop.expeditions.active}}
			{{> "stonetop.gm-expedition-card"}}
			{{/each}}
		</ul>
		{{else if stonetop.expeditions.completed.length}}
		{{!-- Two empty states, because "nothing here yet" and "you have run everything you
		      prepared" are different facts and the second one is wrong advice: what a GM most
		      likely wants is to lift one back out of the fold two inches below, so this one is a
		      quiet line rather than the centred block. --}}
		<p class="stonetop-gm-encounter-empty">{{localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.emptyAllDone"}}</p>
		{{else}}
		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-empty" view="expeditions" kind="stonetop-gm-encounter"
		    title=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.emptyTitle")
		    text=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.empty")
		    label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.add")
		    accepts=stonetop.expeditions.accepts}}
		{{/if}}

		{{!-- COMPLETED, rendered only when there is something in it, so an untouched pane shows one
		      list and not two. It folds, and starts OPEN like every other section on this sheet;
		      the caret rides ON THE HEADING because this section has no pencil of its own, and the
		      heading is the same small-caps eyebrow with its count that Encounters draws. The
		      heading's FOLLOWING SIBLINGS are what the fold hides (`_sectionFoldTargets`), so the
		      box around this pair is load-bearing and a SECOND heading in it would stop the caret
		      claiming at the first.

		      ITS COLLAPSE KEY IS ITS OWN. That preference is stored per user keyed by the id in
		      `collapse=`, so sharing the encounters tab's key would fold both folds together. --}}
		{{#if stonetop.expeditions.completed.length}}
		<div class="stonetop-gm-encounters-completed">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.expeditions.completed")
			    note=stonetop.expeditions.completed.length
			    headingClass="stonetop-move-group-title stonetop-gm-fold-eyebrow"
			    collapse="gm-expeditions-completed"}}
			<ul class="stonetop-gm-encounter-list stonetop-gm-encounter-list--completed">
				{{#each stonetop.expeditions.completed}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-expedition-card"}}
				{{/each}}
			</ul>
		</div>
		{{/if}}

	</section>
</div>
